Another Java glob nuance: in Java globs, within `[...]`, a `-` at the start or end is literal, and the `!` negation. The Dart port doesn't handle the `[a-z]` escaping nuance of a leading `]` (e.g. `[]abc]` in Java glob — actually in Java globs, `]` cannot be first). Minor.

Java glob: `/` matching — in Java, `*` doesn't cross boundaries; `**` does. Dart: same.

